# .env example for GLOS
#
# ON A LAPTOP NOTHING HERE NEEDS SETTING. Every secret has a value printed in the source so that a sandbox works with
# no setup, and the server uses it while GLOS_ENV is not "production".
#
# OUTSIDE A SANDBOX (GLOS_ENV=production) THE SERVER DOES NOT START until each secret in section 2 is set to its own
# random value. This file used to carry the printed values with "CHANGE IN PRODUCTION" beside them; a copy of it would
# have started a live server on secrets anybody could read. The values are no longer here, and the server refuses them.

NODE_ENV=development

# --- 1. Backend basics (04_generated_sandbox/backend) ---
# Port the NestJS API listens on (default 3000). The API is served under /v1.
PORT=3000

# "production" turns the sandbox conveniences off: one-time codes and reset codes are no longer handed back to the
# caller, the open token grant closes, the API docs page is not served, and the secrets below are required.
# GLOS_ENV=production

# --- 2. The secrets the server will not start without, outside a sandbox ---
# Make each one separately with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Each must be 32 characters or more, not a value printed in the source, and not the same as another.
# The two peppers and the vault key must never change afterwards: changing one re-keys what is already stored.
#
# Signs every sign-in token. Whoever has it can sign in as anybody, network staff included.
# GLOS_AUTH_SECRET=
# Seals the identity vault (national ID numbers and other personal data kept encrypted).
# GLOS_VAULT_KEY=
# Keys the hash every phone number is stored as.
# GLOS_PHONE_PEPPER=
# Keys the prints that find a second registration of the same national ID.
# GLOS_IDENTITY_PEPPER=
# Signs payment confirmations on the stand-in payment rail.
# GLOS_FUNDING_SECRET=
# Signs parcel labels.
# GLOS_LABEL_KEY=
# Keys single-field waybill proofs.
# GLOS_DISCLOSURE_KEY=

# --- 3. Who may reach it ---
# Behind a proxy or a load balancer: how many hops to trust ("1"), or which ("loopback, 10.0.0.0/8"). Without it every
# caller looks like one address, and the per-caller limits on sign-in count everybody together.
# GLOS_TRUST_PROXY=1
# Where the apps and the console are served from. Browsers on these sites may call the API; other websites may call
# only the shipping API (what a store's own page uses). Extra sites of ours go in GLOS_CORS_ORIGINS, comma-separated.
# SBG_PUBLIC_URL=https://example.com
# SBG_CONSOLE_URL=https://console.example.com
# GLOS_CORS_ORIGINS=
# The networks network staff work on (addresses or ranges, comma-separated). Unset: staff may sign in from anywhere.
# GLOS_STAFF_NETWORKS=
# The trusted-caller grant (scripts, seeds), and the console's setup key. Outside a sandbox the grant is closed until
# this is set, and it makes a network staff account only while fewer than two people can sign in: the first two.
# After that one member of staff asks for a new account and a second approves it, and this key adds none.
# GLOS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- 4. The code to a phone: Twilio (a sandbox never texts, whatever is set here) ---
# Off a sandbox a code reaches a phone as a text and no other way: without all three of an account, a credential and a
# sender, nobody can sign up, confirm a new phone or replace a PIN. See backend/README.md, "The code to a phone".
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# A credential: an API key and its secret (it can be revoked without touching the account), or the account's own token.
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Who a text is from: a Messaging Service, or one number / sender name.
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=
# TWILIO_FROM=
# Which countries a code is texted to is not set here: it is the countries switched on in the console (Where we
# operate). Twilio keeps a list of its own that cannot be changed for you: switch on the same countries, and no
# others, under SMS Geo Permissions in the Twilio console.

# --- 5. Email (not wired on this machine yet) ---
# ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN=
# ZEPTOMAIL_URL=
# ZEPTOMAIL_WEBHOOK_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# --- Frontend (04_generated_sandbox/frontend) ---
# Optional: override the API base the onboarding wizard calls.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000/v1. Set on window as GLOS_API to override at runtime.
